{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s013_3_d2", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(3): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n(3) Nothing in this article shall prevent Parliament from making any law prescribing, in regard to a class or classes of employment or appointment to an office\n\nProhibition of discrimination on grounds of religion, race, caste, sex or place of birth.\n\nEquality of opportunity in matters of public employment.\n\n> 1Added by the Constitution (First Amendment) Act, 1951, s. 2.\n\n> 2Ins. by the Constitution (Ninety-third Amendment) Act, 2005, s. 2 (w.e.f. 20-1-2006).\n\n( _Part III._ — _Fundamental Rights._ — _Arts._ 16—18.)\n\nAbolition of Untouchability.\n\n## Abolition of titles.\n\n1[under the Government of, or any local or other authority within, a State or Union territory, any requirement as to residence within that State or Union territory] prior to such employment or appointment.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19005", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19005_s020", "title": "The advocates welfare fund act, 2001", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "20", "section_title": "The advocates welfare fund act, 2001", "text": "Act: The advocates welfare fund act, 2001 (Act 45 of 2001) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: MEMBERSHIP AND PAYMENT OUT OF ADVOCATES' WELFARE FUND | Section 20: Review**\n\n**20. Review** .—The Trustee Committee may, on its own motion or on an application received from any person interested, within ninety days of the passing of any order by it under the provisions of this Act, review such order, if it was passed under any mistake, whether of fact or of law or in ignorance of any material fact:\n\nProvided that the Trustee Committee shall not pass any order under this section adversely affecting any person unless such person has been given an opportunity of being heard.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2001.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19005?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19005/act.pdf"}
