{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s013_2_d3", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(2): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n(2) No citizen of India shall accept any title from any foreign State.\n\n> 1Subs. by the Constitution (Seventh Amendment) Act, 1956, s. 29 and Sch., for \"under any State specified in the First Schedule or any local or other authority within its territory, any requirement as to residence within that State\".\n\n> 2Ins. by the Constitution (Seventy-seventh Amendment) Act, 1995, s. 2.\n\n> 3Subs. by the Constitution (Eighty-fifth Amendment) Act, 2001, s. 2, for certain words (w.e.f. 17-6-1995).\n\n> 4Ins. by the Constitution (Eighty-first Amendment) Act, 2000, s. 2 (w.e.f. 9-6-2000).\n\n## ( _Part III._ — _Fundamental Rights._ — _Arts._ 18-19.)", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19013", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19013_s061", "title": "The regiatrstion act, 1908", "chapter": "", "section_number": "61", "section_title": "The regiatrstion act, 1908", "text": "Act: The regiatrstion act, 1908 (Act 16 of 1908) | India | State | In Force\nSection 61: Endorsements and certificate to be copied and document returned.** —( _1_ ) The endorsements and cer\n\n**61. Endorsements and certificate to be copied and document returned.** —( _1_ ) The endorsements and certificate referred to and mentioned in sections 59 and 60 shall thereupon be copied into the margin of the Register-book, and the copy of the map or plan (if any) mentioned in section 21 shall be filed in Book No. 1.\n\n( _2_ ) The registration of the document shall thereupon be deemed complete, and the document shall then be returned to the person who presented the same for registration, or to such other person (if any) as he has nominated in writing in that behalf on the receipt mentioned in section 52.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1908.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19013?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19013/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s122", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "VIII", "section_number": "122", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VIII: CONTROL OF TRAFFIC** | Section 122: Leaving vehicle in dangerous position** - No person in charge of a motor vehicle shall cause or allo\n\n**122. Leaving vehicle in dangerous position** - No person in charge of a motor vehicle shall cause or allow the vehicle or any trailer to be abandoned or to remain at rest on any public place in such a position or in such a condition or in such circumstances as to cause or likely to cause danger, obstruction or undue inconvenience to other users of the public place or to the passengers.\n\n_**Corresponding Law** ._ - Section 122 corresponds to section 81 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons** . -_ Clause 122 lays down that no motor vehicle should be left on the public road in a dangerous position or in such a manner so as to cause inconvenience to other road users or abandoned.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19011", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19011_s32A", "title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "32A", "section_title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "text": "Act: The plantations labour act, 1951 (Act 69 of 1951) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: LEAVE WITH WAGES | Section 32A: Notice of accident**\n\n**32A. Notice of accident** .—Where in any plantation, an accident occurs which causes death or which causes any bodily injury to a worker by reason of which the worker injured is prevented from working for a period of forty-eight hours or more immediately following the accident, or which is of such a nature as may be prescribed in this behalf, the employer thereof shall send notice thereof to such authorities, in such form, and within such time, as may be prescribed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1951.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19011?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19011/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s07B_3", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "7B", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ``` | Section 7B(3): ```\n\n(3) No person shall be appointed under sub-section (1), sub-\nsection (2) 1*[sub-section (2A)] or sub-section (5) or, having been so\nappointed, shall continue to hold officer, who is or becomes directly\nor indirectly interested in a factory or in any process or business\ncarried on therein or in any patent or machinery connected therewith.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 3, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19019", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19019_s026_p0", "title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "26", "section_title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "text": "Act: The inland vessels act, 1917 (Act 1 of 1917) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: MASTERS [INCLUDING SERANGS] AND ENGINEERS [INCLUDING ENGINE-DRIVERS] OR INLAND 1[MECI IANICALLY PROPELLED VESSELS] | Section 26: Certificates to be held by master and engineer of vessel of between forty and one hundred horse-powe\n\n**26. Certificates to be held by master and engineer of vessel of between forty and one hundred horse-power.** —An inland[1] [mechanically propelled vessel] having engines of[10] [forty] or more nominal horse-power, but of less than[6] [one hundred] nominal horse-power, shall not proceed on any voyage unless she has—\n\n( _a_ ) as her master a person possessing a second-class master‟s certificate granted under this Act, or any certificate referred to in clause ( _a_ ) of section 25, and\n\n( _b_ ) as her engineer a person possessing a first-class engine-driver‟s certificate granted under this Act, or an engine-driver‟s[7] [certificate granted or deemed to be granted under the Merchant Shipping Act, 1958 (44 of 1958)] or any certificate referred to in clause ( _b_ ) of section 25:\n\nProvided that a[1] [mechanically propelled vessel] shall be deemed to have complied with this section if she has as her master and engineer a person possessing both a certificate referred to in clause ( _a_ ), and a certificate referred to in clause ( _b_ ), of this section.\n\n> 1. Subs. by Act 35 of 1977, s. 5, for \"steam-vessel\" (w.e.f. 1-5-1978).\n\n> 2. Subs. by Act 11 of 1923, s. 2 and First Schedule, for \"as to such Government\".\n\n> 3. Subs. by the A. 0. 1937, for \"in its discretion\".\n\n> 4. Ins. by Act 6 of 1920. s. 2.\n\n> 5. Ins. by s. 4, _ibid_ .\n\n> 6. Subs. by s. 4, _ibid_ ., for \"eighty\".\n\n> 7. Subs. by Act 35 of 1977, s. 19, for certain words (w.e.f. 1-5-1978).\n\n> 8. Ins. by Act 6 of 1920, s. 5.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Merchant Shipping Act, 1958"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1917.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19019?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19019/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18984", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18984_s026", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "chapter": "I", "section_number": "26", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012 (Act 3 of 2012) | India | State | In Force\nChapter I: ' | Section 26: The District Magistrate or any other officer authorised by him may, by a notice in writing to the li\n\n26. The District Magistrate or any other officer authorised by him may, by a notice in writing to the licensee, require that any sliop in which any liquor is sold shall be closed at such times or for suc~ period as he may think necessary, for preservation of public peace:\n\nClosure of shops for preservation of public peace.\n\nProvided that the closure days in. the licensing year shall not exceed seven days in all or more than three days continuously at anyone time:\n\nProvided further that if the Excise Commissioner or an officer authorised by him in this behalf is of the opinion that any particular shop or all shops in any particular 'area shall be closed for a period exceeding seven days in a licensing year, or more than three days continuously at anyone time, he may with prior sanction of the Administrator, permit to do so.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2012.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18984?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "