{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s215_4", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIV", "section_number": "215", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIV: ** | Section 215(4): Road Safety Councils and Committees.** - (1) The Central Government may, by notification in the Offi\n\n(4) The Councils and Committees referred to in this section shall discharge such functions relating to the road safety programmes as the Central Government or the State Government, as the case may be, may, having regard to the objects of the Act, specify.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - This is a new provisions in the 1988 Act.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 216 seeks to empower the Central Government to constitute a National Road Safety Council and the State Government to constitute a State Safety Council for the State and District Road Safety Committee for the districts consisting of a Chairman and such other members as that Government consider necessary on such terms and conditions as that Government may determine.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s042_p1", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "42", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 42: In section 60 of the principal Act, after sub-section (2), the following sub-sectlon shall be inserted, namely:-\n\n(d) sub-section _(4)_ shall be omitted.\n\n. **45.** In section 62 of the principal Act, for the words and figures \"Subject to t;he provisions of section 61, the State Government\", the w.ord~ \"Th~ C~1J.tral Government\" shall be sul;istituted.\n\nAmendment of section 57.\n\nAmendment of section _59._\n\nAmendment of section 60.\n\nInseution of new section 60A. Reward to persons.\n\nAmendment of section _**(H.**_\n\nAmendment of section 62.\n\n_Wild_ Life _(Protection) Amendment_ [ACT M\n\nAmendment **of** section 63.\n\nAmendmerit of section 64.\n\nAmeJndment of section 66.\n\n**46.** In section 63 of the principal Act, for sub-section _(1),_ the following sub-section shall be substituted, namely:\n\n·\\\n\n\"(1) The Central Government may, by notification, make rules for all or any of the following matters, namely:-\n\n_(a)_ conditions and other matters subject to which **a** license.e may keep any specified plant in his custody or posses1ion under section 17F;\n\n(b) the salaries and allowances and other conditions **of** appointment of chairperson, meml;,ers and member-secreta,ry under sub-section (5) of section 3GB;\n\n( c) the terms and conditions of service of the officers **and** other employees of the Central Zoo Authority under su};). section (7) of section 38H;\n\n(d) the form in which the annual statement of accounts of the Central Zoo Authority shall be prepared under sub~ection _(4)_ of section 38E;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "i