{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s17C_p0", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "17C", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 17C: (l) No person shall cultivate a specified plant except under and in accordance with a licence grante\n\n17C. (l) No person shall cultivate a specified plant except under and in accordance with a licence granted by the Chief Wild **Life** Warden or any other o:ffi:cer authodsed by the State Government in this belialf:\n\nProvided that nothing in this section shall prevent a person, **who,** immediately before the commencement of the Wild Life · (Protection) Amendment Act, 1991, was cultivating a specified plant, from carrying on such cultivation for a period **.of·** six months from such commencement, or where he has made an application within that period for the grant of a licence to him, until the licence is grnnted to him or he is informed in writirig that a licence cannot be granted to him. . (2) Every licence graned under this section sall specify the area in which and the conditions, if any, subject to which **the licen-** see shall cultivate a s-peci:fied plant. · 17D. _(1)_ No person sha'11, except under and in accordance with a licence granted by the Chief Wild Life Warden or any other officer authorised iby the State Government in this behalf, commence, or carry on business or occupation as a dealer in a spec;.ified plant or part or derivate thereof: ·\n\n_Wiid Life (Protection) Amend,ment_", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "d