{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s009_p0", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 9: In section 35 of the principal Act,\n\n19. In section 35 of the principal Act,\n\n_(i)_ for sub-sections _(5)_ and _(6)_ , the following sub-sections shall be substituted, namely:\n\n\" _(5)_ No alteration of the boundaries of a National Park by the State Government-shall be made except on a recommendation of the National Board.\n\n_(6)_ No person shall destroy, exploit or remove any Wild Life including forest produce from a National Park or destroy or damage or divert the habitat of any wild animal by any act whatsoever or divert, stop or enhance the flow of water into or outside the National Park, except under and in accordance with a permit granted by the Chief Wild Life Warden, and no such permit shall be granted unless the State Government being satisfied in consultation with the National Board that such removal of wild life from the National Park or the change in the flow of water into or outside the National Park is necessary for the improvement and better management of wild life therein, authorises the issue of such permit:\n\nProvided that where the forest produce is removed from a National Park, the same may be used for meeting the personal _bona fide_ needs of the people living in and around the National Park and shall not be used for any commercial purpose.\";\n\n_(ii)_ after sub-section _(8)_ , the following _Explanation_ shall be inserted, namely:", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s58B_p1", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "58B", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 58B: In this Chapter, unless the context otherwise requires,\n\n_(2)_ the value of the assets contributed by such person (including the value of the assets, if any, contributed by him earlier) to the trust amounts on the date on which contribution is made, to not less than twenty per cent of the value of the assets of the trust on that date;\n\n_(vi)_ where the competent authority, for reasons to be recorded in writing, considers that any properties of such person are held on his behalf by any other person, such other person;\n\n_(c)_ \"competent authority\" means an officer authorised under section 58D;\n\n_(d)_ \"concealment\" means the concealment or disguise of the nature, source disposition, movement or ownership of property and includes the movement or conversion of such property by electronic transmission or by any other means;\n\n_(e)_ \"freezing\" means temporarily prohibiting the transfer, conversion, disposition or movement of property by an, order issued under section 58F;\n\n_(f)_ \"identifying' includes establishment of proof that the property was derived from, or used in, the illegal hunting and trade of wild life and its products;\n\n_(g)_ \"illegally acquired property\" in relation to any person to whom this Chapter applies, means\n\n_(i)_ any property acquired by such person, wholly or partly out of or by means of any income earnings or assets derived or obtained from or attributable to illegal hunting and trade of wild life and its products and derivatives;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "general", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Companies Act 1956"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18989", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18989_s034", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "chapter": "XVII", "section_number": "34", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966 (Act 2 of 1966) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XVII: Miscellaneous** | Section 34: Satinwood (Murraya exoitica)\n\n34. Satinwood (Murraya exoitica).\n\n## **S.RADHAKRISHANA**\n\n**President.**\n\n## **S.P.SENVARMA,**\n\n_**Secy. to the Govt. of India**_", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "general", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1966.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18989?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18989/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19015", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19015_s037", "title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "37", "section_title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "text": "Act: The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016 (Act 49 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: SPECIAL PROVISIONS FOR PERSONS WITH BENCHMARK DISABILITES | Section 37: Special schemes and development programmes.** —The appropriate Government and the local authorities shall, by notification, make schemes in favour of persons with benchmark disabilities, to provide,—\n\n**37. Special schemes and development programmes.** —The appropriate Government and the local authorities shall, by notification, make schemes in favour of persons with benchmark disabilities, to provide,—\n\n( _a_ ) five per cent. reservation in allotment of agricultural land and housing in all relevant schemes and development programmes, with appropriate priority to women with benchmark disabilities;\n\n( _b_ ) five per cent. reservation in all poverty alleviation and various developmental schemes with priority to women with benchmark disabilities;\n\n( _c_ ) five per cent. reservation in allotment of land on concessional rate, where such land is to be used for the purpose of promoting housing, shelter, setting up of occupation, business, enterprise, recreation centres and production centres.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2016.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19015?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19015/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s006_3", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "6", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 6(3): Constitution of the Wildlife Advisory Board\n\n(3) The term of office of the members of the Board referred to in C1.(g) of sub-section (1) and the manner of filling the vacancies among them shall be such as may be prescribed.[ 8]", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
