{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s042", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "42", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: ** | Section 42: Certificate of ownership.** - The Chief Wildlife Warden may, for the purposes of Sec. 40, issue a ce\n\n**42. Certificate of ownership.** - The Chief Wildlife Warden may, for the purposes of Sec. 40, issue a certificate of ownership in such form, as may be prescribed, to any person who, in his opinion, is in lawful possession of any wild animal or any animal article, trophy, or uncured trophy, and may, where possible, mark, in the prescribed manner, such animal article, trophy or uncured trophy for the purposes of Identification.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_20096", "chunk_id": "IND_state_20096_s11C_p3", "title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "11C", "section_title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "text": "Act: The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957 (Act 67 of 1957) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: 7[PROCEDURE FOR OBTAINING MINERAL CONCESSION IN RESPECT OF LAND IN WHICH THE MINERALS | Section 11C: Power of Central Government to amend First Schedule and Fourth Schedule.** ―The Central Government m\n\n> 2. Subs. by Act 38 of 1999, s. 13, for clauses ( _c_ ) and ( _d_ ) (w.e.f. 18-12-1999).", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2021"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1957.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/20096?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_20096/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19011", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19011_s16C", "title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "16C", "section_title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "text": "Act: The plantations labour act, 1951 (Act 69 of 1951) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ## WELFARE | Section 16C: Application for compensation**\n\n**16C. Application for compensation** .—( _1_ ) An application for payment of compensation under section 16A may be made to the Commissioner—\n\n( _a_ ) by the person who has sustained the injury; or\n\n( _b_ ) by any agent duly authorised by the person who has sustained the injury; or\n\n( _c_ ) where the person who has sustained the injury is a minor, by his guardian; or\n\n( _d_ ) where death has resulted out of the collapse of the house, by any dependant of the deceased or\n\nby any agent duly authorised by such dependant or, if such dependant is a minor, by his guardian.\n\n( _2_ ) Every application under sub-section ( _1_ ) shall be in such form and shall contain such particulars as may be prescribed.\n\n( _3_ ) No application for compensation under this section shall be entertained unless it is made within six months of the collapse of the house:\n\nProvided that the Commissioner may, if he is satisfied that the applicant was prevented by sufficient cause from making the application within the aforesaid period of six months, entertain such application within a further period of six months.\n\n_Explanation_ .—In this section, the expression \"dependant\" has the meaning assigned to it in clause ( _d_ ) of section 2 of the Workmen's Compensation Act, 1923 (8 of 1923).", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Compensation Act, 1923"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1951.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19011?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19011/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s38E_2", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "38E", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ** | Section 38E(2): Grants and loans to Authority and constitution of found.** - (1) The Central Government may, after d\n\n(2) There shall be constituted a Fund to be called the Central Zoo Authority Fund and there shall be credited thereto any grants and loans made to the Authority by the Central Government all fees and charges received by the Authority under this Act and all sums received by the Authority from such other sources as may be decided upon by the Central Government.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s013_3", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(3): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n(3) Without prejudice to the powers conferred on the Supreme Court by clauses (1) and (2), Parliament may by law empower any other court to exercise within the local limits of its jurisdiction all or any of the powers exercisable by the Supreme Court under clause (2).", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s010_p0", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "10", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 10: **Amendment of bye-laws of co-operative society** :- 1) No amendment of any\n\n10. **Amendment of bye-laws of co-operative society** :- 1) No amendment of any\n\nbye-laws of a co-operative society shall be valid until the same has been registered under this Regulation.\n\n**6**\n\n2) Every proposal for such amendment shall be forwarded to the Registrar in the prescribed manner and if the Registrar is satisfied that the proposed amendment:-\n\n- (i) is not contrary to this Regulation or to the rules:\n\n- (ii) does not conflict with co-operative principles; and\n\n- (iii) will promote the economic interests of the members of the society, he may register the amendment;\n\nProvided that not order refusing to register the amendment of bye-laws shall be passed except after giving the co-operative society an opportunity of making its representation.\n\n3) The Registrar shall forward to the co-operative society a copy of the registered amendment together with a certificate signed by him and such certificate shall be conclusive evidence that the amendment has been duly registered,\n\n4) Where the Registrar refuses to register an amendment of the bye-laws of a\n\nco-operative society, he shall communicate the order of refusal together with the reasons therefore, to the society in the prescribed manner.\n\n5) An amendment of the bye-laws of a registered society shall take effect from the date, if any, specified in the amendment and where no such date is specified, the amendment shall take effect from the date on which it is registered.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
