{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s103_2_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "103", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 103(2): Issue of permits to State transport undertakings. -** (1) Where, in pursuance of an approved scheme,\n\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), no compensation shall be payable on account of the cancellation of any existing permit or any modification of the terms thereof, when a permit for an alternative route or area in lieu thereof has been offered by the State Transport Authority or the Regional Transport Authority, as the case may be and accepted by the holder of the permit.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s110_2_d2", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "110", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 110(2): Power of Central Government to make rules.** - (1) The Central Government may make rules regulating\n\n(2) Rules may be made under sub-section (1) governing the matters mentioned therein, including the manner of ensuring the compliance with such matters and the maintenance of motor vehicles in respect of such matters, either\n\ngenerally in respect of motor vehicles or trailers or in respect of motor vehicles or trailers of a particular class or in particular circumstances.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s22F", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "22F", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 22F: Application of Payment of Wages Act, 1936, to scheduled employments\n\n22F. Application of Payment of Wages Act, 1936, to scheduled employments.- (1) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Payment of Wages Act, 1936 (4 of 1936). the appropriate Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, direct that, subject to the provisions of sub-section (2), all or any of the provisions of the said Act shall with such modifications, if any, as may be specified in the notification, apply to wages payable to employees in such scheduled employments as may be specified in the notification. (2) Where all or any of the provisions of the said Act are applied to wages payable to employees in any scheduled employment under sub-section (1), the Inspector appointed under this Act shall be deemed to be the Inspector for the purpose of enforcement of the provisions so applied within the local limits of his jurisdiction.]\n\n23.\n\nExemption of employer from liability in certain cases.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Wages Act, 1936"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18989", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18989_s070_4", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "70", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966 (Act 2 of 1966) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ASSESSMENT AND RE-ASSESSMENT OF LAND IN URBAN AREAS** | Section 70(4): The area and assessment of plot numbers and sub-divisions of plot number shall be entered in such records as may be prescribed\n\n(4) The Chief Commissioner may approve the standard rates submitted to him under sub-section (3) with such modification if any as he may consider necessary.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1966.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18989?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18989/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18989", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18989_s002_p0", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "chapter": "XVI", "section_number": "2", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966 (Act 2 of 1966) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XVI: ** | Section 2: (1) Any person who unauthorisedly takes or remains in possession of any unoccupied land or abadi may\n\n202. (1) Any person who unauthorisedly takes or remains in possession of any unoccupied land or abadi may be summarily ejected by order of the Tehsildar and any crop which may be standing on the land and any building or other work which he may have constructed thereon, if not removed by him within such times as the Tehsildar may fix, shall be liable to forfeiture.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1966.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18989?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18989/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s201", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIII", "section_number": "201", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIII: ** | Section 201: Penalty for causing obstruction to free flow of traffic.** - (1) Whoever keeps a disabled vehicle on\n\n**201. Penalty for causing obstruction to free flow of traffic.** - (1) Whoever keeps a disabled vehicle on any public place, in such a manner, so as to cause impediment to the free flow of traffic, shall be liable for penalty up to fifty rupees per hour, so long as it remains in that position :\n\nProvided that the vehicle involved in accidents shall be liable for penalty only from the time of completion of inspection formalities under the law :\n\n9[Provided further that where the vehicle is removed by a Government agency, towing charges shall be recovered from the vehicle owner or person in-charge of such vehicle.]\n\n10[(2) Penalties or towing charges under this section shall be recovered by such officer or authority as the State Government may, by notification in the Official Gazette, authorise.]\n\n_**Corresponding Law-**_ This is a new provision in the 1988 Act.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons-**_ Clause 201 lays down penalty for keeping a disabled vehicle on public road causing impediment to the free flow of traffic.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s020", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "20", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: ``` | Section 20: Spittoons. (1) In every factory there shall be provided a\n\n20. Spittoons. (1) In every factory there shall be provided a\nsufficient number of spittoons in convenient places and they shall be\nmaintained in a clean and hygienic condition.\n```\n\n```\n(2) The State Government may make rules prescribing the type and\nthe number of spittoons to be provided and their location in any\nfactory and provide for such further matters relating to their\nmaintenance in a clean and hygienic condition.\n```\n\n```\n(3) No person shall spit within the premises of a factory except\nin the spittoons provided for the purposes and a notice containing\nthis provision and the penalty for its violation shall be prominently\ndisplayed at suitable places in the premises.\n```\n\n```\n(4) Whoever spits in contravention of sub-section (3) shall be\npunishable with fine not exceeding five rupees.\n```\n\n```\nCHAP SAFETY\n```\n\n```\nCHAPTER IV\n```\n\n```\nSAFETY\n```\n\n```\n21.\n```\n\n```\nFencing of machinery.\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s58D", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "58D", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 58D: The State Government may, by order published in the Official Gazette, authorise any officer not belo\n\n58D. The State Government may, by order published in the Official Gazette, authorise any officer not below the rank of Chief Conservator of Forests to perform the functions of the competent authority under this Chapter in respect of such persons or classes of persons as the State Government may, direct.\n\n## **Identifying Illegally Acquired Property**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "order", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_20096", "chunk_id": "IND_state_20096_s11C_p1", "title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "11C", "section_title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "text": "Act: The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957 (Act 67 of 1957) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: 7[PROCEDURE FOR OBTAINING MINERAL CONCESSION IN RESPECT OF LAND IN WHICH THE MINERALS | Section 11C: Power of Central Government to amend First Schedule and Fourth Schedule.** ―The Central Government m\n\n> 3. Subs. by Act 16 of 2021, s. 2, for \"prospecting licence-cum-mining lease\" (w.e.f. 28-3-2021).\n\n> 4. Subs. by s. 7, _ibid_ ., for \"competitive bidding or otherwise\" (w.e.f. 10-1-2020).\n\n> 5. Ins. by Act 10 of 2015, s. 12 (w.e.f. 12-1-2015).\n\n> 6. Ins. by Act 16 of 2023, s. 10 (w.e.f. 17-8-2023).\n\n( _3_ ) The royalty, dead rent, applicable amount quoted in the auction and any other statutory payment in relation to the mining lease or composite licence auctioned by the Central Government shall accrue to the State Government or concerned authorities, as the case may be, as if the auction has been conducted by the State Government.]\n\n**12.**[1] **[Registers of mineral concession** . **]** ―( _1_ ) The State Government shall cause to be maintained in the prescribed form―\n\n( _a_ ) a register of applications for prospecting licences;\n\n( _b_ ) a register of prospecting licensees;\n\n2 [( _c_ ) a register of applications for mining leases;\n\n- ( _d_ ) a register of mining lessees;\n\n( _e_ ) a register of applications for reconnaissance permits;[3] ***\n\n( _f_ ) a register of reconnaissance permits,]\n\n> 4[( _g_ ) a register of applications for exploration licences; and\n\n( _h_ ) a register of exploration licence,]\n\nin each of which shall be entered such particulars as may be prescribed.\n\n( _2_ ) Every such register shall be open to inspection by any person on payment of such fee as the State Government may fix.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2021"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1957.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/20096?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_20096/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19013", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19013_s016", "title": "The regiatrstion act, 1908", "chapter": "", "section_number": "16", "section_title": "The regiatrstion act, 1908", "text": "Act: The regiatrstion act, 1908 (Act 16 of 1908) | India | State | In Force\nSection 16: Register-books and fire-proof boxes**\n\n**16. Register-books and fire-proof boxes** .—( _1_ ) The[1] [State Government] shall provide for the office of every registering officer the books necessary for the purposes of this Act.\n\n( _2_ ) The books so provided shall contain the forms from time to time prescribed by the InspectorGeneral, with the sanction of the[1] [State Government], and the pages of such books shall be consecutively numbered in print, and the number of pages in each book shall be certified on the title page by the officer by whom such books are issued.\n\n( _3_ ) The[1] [State Government] shall supply the office of every Registrar with a fire-proof box, and shall in each district make suitable provision for the safe custody of the records connected with the registration of documents in such district.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1908.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19013?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19013/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s58A", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "58A", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 58A: The provisions of this Chapter shall apply only to the following persons, namely:\n\n## **CHAPTER VI A**\n\n## **FORFEITURE OF PROPERTY DERIVED FROM ILLEGAL HUNTING AND TRADE**\n\n## **Application**\n\n58A. The provisions of this Chapter shall apply only to the following persons, namely:\n\n_(a)_ every person who has been convicted of an offence punishable under this Act with imprisonment for a term of three years or more;\n\n_(b)_ every associate of a person referred to in clause _(a)_ ;\n\n_(c)_ any holder (hereafter in this clause referred to as the present holder) of any property which was at any time previously held by a person referred to in clause _(a)_ or clause _(b)_ unless the present holder or, as the case may be, any one who held such property after such person and before the present holder, is or was a transferee in good faith for adequate consideration.\n\n## **Definition**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
