rce_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19314/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s010", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "10", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: CENTRAL[1] [WAQF] COUNCIL | Section 10: Finance of Council\n\n**10. Finance of Council.—** ( _1_ ) Every Board shall pay from its[1] [Waqf] Fund annually to the Council such contribution as is equivalent to one per cent. of the aggregate of the net annual income of the 2[auqaf] in respect of which contribution is payable under sub-section ( _1_ ) of section 72:\n\nProvided that where the Board, in the case of any particular[1] [waqf] has remitted under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 72 the whole of the contribution payable to it under sub-section ( _1_ ) of that section, then for calculating the contribution payable to the Council under this section the net annual income of the[1] [waqf] in respect of which such remission has been granted shall not be taken into account.\n\n( _2_ ) All monies received by the Council under sub-section ( _1_ ) and all other monies received by it as donations, benefactions and grants shall form a fund to be called the Central[1] [Waqf] Fund.\n\n( _3_ ) Subject to any rules that may be made by the Central Government in this behalf, the Central 1[Waqf] Fund shall be under the control of the Council and may be applied for such purposes as the Council may deem fit.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s003_31", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "", "section_number": "3", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nSection 3(31): \"motorcab\" means any motor vehicle constructed or adapted to carry not more than six passengers excluding the driver for hire or reward ;\n\n(31) \"permit\" means a permit issued by a State or Regional Transport Authority or an authority prescribed in this behalf under this Act authorising the use of motor vehicle as a transport vehicle ;\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 2 (31) corresponds to section 2 (20) of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939", "Road Transport Corporations Act, 1950"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s065_p1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "65", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 65: Power of the State Government to make rules.** - (1) A State Government may make rules for the purpo\n\n(h) the exemption of prescribed persons or prescribed classes of persons from payment of all or any portion of the fees payable under this Chapter.\n\n(i) the forms, other than those prescribed by the Central Government to be used for the purposes of this Chapter;\n\n(j) the communication between registering authorities of particulars of certificates of registration and by owners of vehicles registered outside the State of particulars of such vehicles and of their registration;\n\n(k) the amount or amounts under sub-section (13) of section 41 or sub-section (7) of section 47 or sub-section (4) of section 49 or sub-section (5) of section 50;\n\n(l) the extension of the validity of certificate of fitness pending consideration of applications for their renewal;\n\n(m)the extension from the provisions of this Chapter, and the conditions and fees for exemption, of motor vehicles in the possession of dealers;\n\n(n) the form in which and the period within which the return under section 62 shall be sent;\n\n(o) the manner in which the State Register of Motor Vehicles shall be maintained under section 63;\n\n(p) any other matter which is to be or may be prescribed.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 65 corresponds to section 41 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 65 empowers the State Government to make rules for the purpose of carrying into effect the provisions of this Chapter.\n\n## ***CHAPTER V**\n\n## **CONTROL OF TRANSPORT VEHICLES**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19316", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19316_b000_4_d1", "title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "chapter": "", "section_number": "", "section_title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "text": "Act: The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986 (Act 61 of 1986) | India | State | In Force\n(4): Preamble\n\n(4) No child shall be permitted or required to work between 7 p.m. and 8 a.m.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1948", "Mines Act, 1952", "Merchant Shipping Act, 1958", "Motor Transport Workers Act, 1961", "Plantations Labour Act, 1951", "Children Act, 1938", "Minimum Wages Act, 1948"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1986.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19316?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19316/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s009_d3", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "X", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter X: ** | Section 9: _**Appointment of Presiding Officer and his duties**_ :- The Returning Office - The Returning Office\n\n9. _**Appointment of Presiding Officer and his duties**_ :- The Returning Office - The Returning Office may appoint Presiding Officer for each polling station and also polling officers and polling assistants to assist the Presiding Officer to conduct the poll. The Presiding Officer shall perform such duties as may be prescribed by the Registrar from time to time.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s048_p0", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "48", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: ## MAINTENANCE OF ACCOUNTS OF[2] [AUQAF] | Section 48: Board to pass orders on auditor's report\n\n**48. Board to pass orders on auditor's report.—** ( _1_ ) The Board shall examine the auditor's report, and may call for the explanation of any person in regard to any matter mentioned therein, and shall pass such orders as it thinks fit including orders for the recovery of the amount certified by the auditor under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 47.\n\n( _2_ ) The mutawalli or any other person aggrieved by any order made by the Board may, within thirty days of the receipt by him of the order, apply to the Tribunal to modify or set aside the order and the Tribunal may, after taking such evidence as it may think necessary, confirm or modify the order or remit the amount so certified, either in whole or in part, and may also make such order as to costs as it may think appropriate in the circumstances of the case.\n\n( _3_ ) No application made under sub-section ( _2_ ) shall be entertained by the Tribunal unless the amount certified by the auditor under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 47 has first been deposited in the Tribunal and the Tribunal shall not have any power to stay the operation of the order made by the Board under sub-section ( _1_ ).\n\nTribunal shall not have any power to stay the operation of the order made by the Board under\n\n( _4_ ) The order made by the Tribunal under sub-section ( _2_ ) shall be final.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s001_7", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: .—SPECIAL DIRECTIVES | Section 1(7): to entertain and dispose of appeals and petitions from or in respect of any judgment, decree or order of any court within that State shall cease, and all appeals and other proceedings pending before the said authority at such commencement shall be transferred to, and disposed of by, the Supreme Court.\n\n(7) The High Court for the State shall not have any powers of superintendence over the Administrative Tribunal and no court (other than the Supreme Court) or tribunal shall exercise any jurisdiction, power or authority in respect of any matter subject to the jurisdiction, power or authority of, or in relation to, the Administrative Tribunal.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Bombay Reorganisation Act, 1960", "Nagaland Act, 1962", "India Act, 1935", "States Reorganisation Act, 1956", "The Indian Independence Act, 1947", "Privy Council Jurisdiction Act, 1949"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18984", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18984_s079_7", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "79", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012 (Act 3 of 2012) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: DETECTION, INVESTIGATION AND TRw. OF OFFENcEs | Section 79(7): The Excise Commissioner may, at any time within six months from-the date of the order with a view to\n\n(7) The High Court may determine any issue which-\n\n_(a)_ has not been determined by the Excise Commissioner;\n\n_(b)_ h~ been wrongly determined by the Excise Commissioner, by reason of a decision of such<4uestion of law as is referred to in sub-section (1) .\n\n. ' ~.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2012.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18984?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18984/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s052_p1", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "52", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: AUDIT, INQUIRY, INSPECTION AND SURCHARGE** | Section 52: _**Costs of inquiry and inspection**_ :-Where an inquiry is held under section 50, or an inspection\n\nwinding up of a co-operative society, it is found that any person, who is or was entrusted with the organisation or management of such society or who is or has at any time been an officer or an employee of the society, has made any payment contrary to this Regulation, the rules or the bye-laws or has caused any deficiency in the assets of the society by breach of trust or wilful negligence or has misappropriated or fraudulently retained any money or other property belonging to such society, the Registrar may, of his own motion or on the application of the committee, liquidator or any creditor, inquire himself or direct any person authorised by him, by an order in writing in this behalf, to inquire into the conduct of such person:\n\nProvided that no such inquiry shall be held after the expiry of six years from the date of any act or omission referred to in this sub-section.\n\n(2)Where an inquiry is made under sub-section (1) the Registrar may after giving the person concerned an opportunity of being heard, make an order requiring him to repay or restore the money or property or any part thereof, with interest at such rate, or to pay contribution and costs or compensation to such extent, as the Registrar may consider just and equitable.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s001_4", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 1(4): (/) This Act may be called the Wild Life (Protection) Amendment Act, 2006\n\n(4) The salaries and allowances and other conditions of appointment of the members of the Tiger Conservation Authority shall be such as may be prescribed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s003_35", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "", "section_number": "3", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nSection 3(35): \"motorcab\" means any motor vehicle constructed or adapted to carry not more than six passengers excluding the driver for hire or reward ;\n\n(35) \"public service vehicle\" means any motor vehicle used or adapted to be used for the carriage of passengers for hire or reward, and includes a maxicab, a motorcab, contract carriage, and stage carriage ;\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 2 (35) corresponds to section 2 (25) of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939", "Road Transport Corporations Act, 1950"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18989", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18989_s043", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "43", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966 (Act 2 of 1966) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: REVENUE SURVEY AND SETTLEMENT IN NON URBAN AREAS** | Section 43: The provisions of this Chapter shall apply in respect of lands in non-urban areas\n\n## **CHAPTER VI REVENUE SURVEY AND SETTLEMENT IN NON URBAN AREAS**\n\n43. The provisions of this Chapter shall apply in respect of lands in non-urban areas.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1966.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18989?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18989/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18997", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18997_s018_3_d2", "title": "The contract labour (regulation and abolition) act, 1970", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "18", "section_title": "The contract labour (regulation and abolition) act, 1970", "text": "Act: The contract labour (regulation and abolition) act, 1970 (Act 37 of 1970) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: ** | Section 18(3): Other facilities\n\n(3) Every rule made by the Central Government under this Act shall be laid as soon as may be after it is made, before each House of Parliament while it is in session for a total period of thirty days which may be comprised in one session or in two successive sessions, and if before the expiry of the session in which it is so laid or the session immediately following, both Houses agree in making any modification in the rule or both Houses agree that the rule should not be made, the rule shall thereafter have effect only in such modified form or be of no effect, as the case may be; so, however, that any such modification or annulment shall be without prejudice to the validity of anything previously done under that rule.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Criminal Procedure Code, 1973"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1970.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18997?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18997/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19015", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19015_s001_p0", "title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "chapter": "I", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "text": "Act: The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016 (Act 49 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter I: PRELIMINARY | Section 1: 19th April, 2017, _vide_ notification no. S.O. 1215 (E) dated 19th April, 2017, _see_ Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3 (ii)\n\n> 1. 19th April, 2017, _vide_ notification no. S.O. 1215 (E) dated 19th April, 2017, _see_ Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3 (ii).\n\n( _d_ ) \"care-giver\" means any person including parents and other family Members who with or without payment provides care, support or assistance to a person with disability;\n\n( _e_ ) \"certifying authority\" means an authority designated under sub-section ( _1_ ) of section 57;\n\n( _f_ ) \"communication\" includes means and formats of communication, languages, display of text, Braille, tactile communication, signs, large print, accessible multimedia, written, audio, video, visual displays, sign language, plain-language, human-reader, augmentative and alternative modes and accessible information and communication technology;\n\n( _g_ ) \"competent authority\" means an authority appointed under section 49;\n\n( _h_ ) \"discrimination\" in relation to disability, means any distinction, exclusion, restriction on the basis of disability which is the purpose or effect of impairing or nullifying the recognition, enjoyment or exercise on an equal basis with others of all human rights and fundamental freedoms in the political, economic, social, cultural, civil or any other field and includes all forms of discrimination and denial of reasonable accommodation;\n\n( _i_ ) \"establishment\" includes a Government establishment and private establishment;\n\n( _j_ ) \"Fund\" means the National Fund constituted under section 86;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Companies Act, 2013", "Cantonments Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2016.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19015?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19015/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s001_3_d10", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: .—SPECIAL DIRECTIVES | Section 1(3): to entertain and dispose of appeals and petitions from or in respect of any judgment, decree or order of any court within that State shall cease, and all appeals and other proceedings pending before the said authority at such commencement shall be transferred to, and disposed of by, the Supreme Court.\n\n(3) Nothing in this Constitution shall operate to invalidate the exercise of jurisdiction by His Majesty in Council to dispose of appeals and petitions from, or in respect of, any judgment, decree or order of any court within the territory of India in so far as the exercise of such jurisdiction is authorised by law, and any order of His Majesty in Council made on any such appeal or petition after the commencement of this Constitution shall for all purposes have effect as if it were an order or decree made by the Supreme Court in the exercise of the jurisdiction conferred on such Court by this Constitution.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Bombay Reorganisation Act, 1960", "Nagaland Act, 1962", "India Act, 1935", "States Reorganisation Act, 1956", "The Indian Independence Act, 1947", "Privy Council Jurisdiction Act, 1949"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s041_14_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "41", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 41(14): Registration, how to be made.** - (1) An application by or on behalf of the owner of a motor vehicle\n\n**officers, etc.** - (1) Where an application for registration of a motor vehicle is made under sub-section (1) of section 41 by or on behalf of any diplomatic officer or consular officer, then notwithstanding anything contained in sub section (3) or sub-section (6) of that section, the registering authority shall register the vehicle in such manner and in accordance with such procedure as may be provided by\n\nrules made in this behalf by the Central Government under sub-section (3) and shall assign to the vehicle for display thereon a special registration mark in accordance with the provisions contained in those rules and shall issue a certificate ( hereafter in this\n\n20. Substituted for \"original registering authority\" by Act 54 of 1994, S.14 (w.e.f. 14-11 1994).\n\nsection referred to as the certificate of registration ) that the vehicle has been registered under this section ; and any vehicle so registered shall not, so long as it remains the property of any diplomatic officer or consular officer, require to be registered otherwise under this Act.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s017_3_d1", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "17", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 17(3): Minimum time rate wages for piece work\n\n(b) examine any person whom he finds in any such premises or place and who, he has reasonable cause to believe, is an employee employed therein or an employee to whom work is given out therein;\n\n(c) require any person giving out-work and any out-workers, to give any information, which is in his power to give, with respect to the names and addresses of the persons to, for and from whom the work is given out or received, and with respect to the payments to be made for the work;\n\n1*[(d) seize or take copies of such register, record of wages or notices or portions thereof as he may consider relevant in respect of an offence under this Act which he has reason to believe has been committed by an employer; and]\n\n(e) exercise such other powers as may be prescribed. --------------------------------------------------------------------1. Subs. by Act 30 of 1957, s. 11, for the original clause. 212", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1934"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19012", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19012_s086_p1", "title": "The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016", "chapter": "X", "section_number": "86", "section_title": "The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016", "text": "Act: The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016 (Act 17 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter X: ## MISCELLANEOUS | Section 86: Laying of rules**\n\n( _2_ ) Every rule made by a State Government or the Union territory Government, as the case may be, every regulation made by the Authority under the State Government or the Union territory Government of Puducherry, as the case may be, and every notification issued by the State Government or the Union territory Government of Puducherry, as the case may be, under this Act, shall be laid as soon as may be, after it is made, before the State Legislature, or the Union territory Legislature, as the case may be, where it consists of two Houses, or where such legislature consists of one House, before that House.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2016.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19012?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19012/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s059_2_d1", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "IX", "section_number": "59", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IX: ** | Section 59(2): _**Powers of liquidator**_ :- (1) Subject to any rules made in this behalf, the\n\n- (g) to give such directions in regard to the collection and distribution of the assets of the co-operative society as may appear to him to be necessary for the winding up of its affairs ;\n\n- (h) to carry on the business of the co-operative society so far as may be necessary for its beneficial winding up ;\n\n- (i) to make any compromise or arrangement with creditors or persons claiming to be creditors or having or alleging to have any claim, present or future, whereby the co-operative society may be rendered liable;\n\n- (j) to make any compromise or arrangements with any person between whom and the co-operative society there exists any dispute and to refer any such dispute to arbitration ;\n\n- (k) after consulting the members of the co-operative society, to dispose of the surplus, if any, remaining after paying the claims against the society, in such manners as may be prescribed ; and", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Credit Guarantee Corporation Act, 1961", "India Act, 1934"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s009_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 9: Sub-S. (2) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 28 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (2) read as under :-\n\n59. Sub-S. (2) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 28 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (2) read as under :-\n\n\"(2) The State Government shall constitute for the State, a State Transport Appellate Tribunal which shall consist of a judicial officer who is not below the rank of a District Judge, or who is qualified to be a judge of a High Court :\n\nProvided that in relation to a Union territory, the Tribunal may consist of the Administrator of that territory or any officer who has judicial experience\".\n\nappeal lies, and if it appears to the State Transport Appellate Tribunal that the order made by the State Transport Authority or Regional Transport Authority is improper or illegal, the State Transport Appellate Tribunal may pass such order in relation to the case as it deems fit and every such order shall be final :\n\nProvided that the State Transport Appellate Tribunal shall not entertain any application from a person aggrieved by an order of a State Transport Authority or Regional Transport Authority, unless the application is made within thirty days from the date of the order :\n\nProvided further that the State Transport Appellate Tribunal may entertain the application after the expiry of the said period of thirty days, if it is satisfied that the\n\napplicant was prevented by good and sufficient cause from making the application in time :", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s132_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "VIII", "section_number": "132", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VIII: CONTROL OF TRAFFIC** | Section 132: Duty of driver to stop in certain cases. -** (1) The driver of motor vehicle shall cause the vehicle\n\n**132. Duty of driver to stop in certain cases. -** (1) The driver of motor vehicle shall cause the vehicle to stop & remain stationary so long as 79[may for such reasonable time as may be necessary, but not exceeding twenty-four hours],-\n\n80[(a) when required to do so by any police officer not below the rank of a Sub-Inspector in uniform, in the event of the vehicle being involved in the occurrence of an accident to a person, animal or vehicle or of damage to property, or]\n\n(b) when required to do so by any person in charge of an animal if such person apprehends that the animal is, or being alarmed by the vehicle will become, unmanageable, or\n\n(c) 79 **8** 10[***]\n\nAnd he shall give his name and address and the name and address of the owner of the vehicle to any person affected by any such accident or damage who demands it provided such person also furnishes his name and address.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s023_3", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "23", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 23(3): Effect of disqualification order.** - (1) A person in respect of whom any disqualification order is\n\n(3) Any person in respect of whom any disqualification order has been made may at any time after the expiry of six months from the date of the order, apply to the Court or other authority by which the order was made, to remove the disqualification ; and the Court or authority, as the case may be, may having regard to all the circumstances, either cancel or vary the disqualification order :\n\nProvided that where the Court or other authority refuses to cancel or vary any disqualification order under this section, a second application thereunder shall not be entertained before the expiry of a period of three months from the date of such refusal.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 23 corresponds to section 18 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 23 lays down that on the orders of the Courts disqualifying the holder of the licence, the licence shall cease to be effective.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
