{"act_id": "IND_state_19011", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19011_s008", "title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "8", "section_title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "text": "Act: The plantations labour act, 1951 (Act 69 of 1951) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: PROVISIONS AS TO HEALTH | Section 8: Drinking water**\n\n## CHAPTER III\n\nPROVISIONS AS TO HEALTH\n\n**8. Drinking water** .—In every plantation effective arrangements shall be made by the employer to provide and maintain at convenient places in the plantation a sufficient supply of wholesome drinking water for all workers.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1951.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19011?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19011/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s009_d1", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 9: In section 11 of the principal Act, in sub-section _(1)_ ,\n\n9. In section 11 of the principal Act, in sub-section _(1)_ ,\n\n_(i)_ in clause _(a)_ , the following provisos and _Explanation_ thereunder shall be inserted, namely:\n\n\"Provided that no wild animal shall be ordered to be killed unless the Chief Wild Life Warden is satisfied that such animal cannot be captured, tranquilised or translocated:\n\nProvided further that no such captured animal shall be kept in captivity unless the Chief Wild Life Warden is satisfied that such animal cannot be rehabilitated in the wild and the reasons for the same are recorded in writing.\n\n_Explanation_ For the purposes of clause (a), the process or capture or translocation, as the case may be, of such animal shall be made in such manner as to cause minimum trauma to the said animal.\";\n\n_(ii)_ in clause _(b),_ for the words \"such animal or cause such animal to be hunted\", the words \"such animal or group of animals in a specified area or cause such animal or group of animals in that specified area to be hunted\" shall be substituted.\n\n## **Substitution of Heading of Chapter IV**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s100_3", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "100", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 100(3): Objection to the proposal. -** (1) On the publication of any proposal regarding a scheme in the Offi\n\n(3) The scheme relating to the proposal as approved or modified under sub section (2) shall then be published in the Official Gazette by the State Government making such scheme and in not less than one newspaper in the regional language circulating in the area or route covered by such scheme and the same shall thereupon become final on the date of its publication in the Official Gazette and shall be called the approved scheme and the area or route to which it relates shall be called the notified area or notified route ;\n\nProvided that no such scheme which relates to any inter-State route shall be deemed to be an approved scheme unless it has the previous approval of the Central Government.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19024", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19024_s016", "title": "The maternity benefit act, 1961", "chapter": "", "section_number": "16", "section_title": "The maternity benefit act, 1961", "text": "Act: The maternity benefit act, 1961 (Act 53 of 1961) | India | State | In Force\nSection 16: Inspectors to be public servants\n\n**16. Inspectors to be public servants.—** Every Inspector appointed under this Act shall be deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of section 21 of the Indian Penal Code (45 of 1860).", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1961.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19024?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19024/act.pdf"}
