{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s026_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "26", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 26: Maintenance of State Registers of Driving Licences.** - (1) Each State Government shall maintain, in\n\n**26. Maintenance of State Registers of Driving Licences.** - (1) Each State Government shall maintain, in such form as may be prescribed by the Central Government, a register to be known as the State Register of Driving Licences, in respect of driving llicences issued and renewed by the licensing authorities of the State Government, containing the following particulars, namely :-\n\n- (a) names and addresses of holders of driving licences ;\n\n- (b) licence numbers ;\n\n- (c) dates of issue or renewal of licences ;\n\n- (d) dates of expiry of licences ;\n\n- (e) classes and types of vehicles authorised to be driven ; and\n\n(f) such other particulars as the Central government may prescribe.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
