{"act_id": "IND_state_19026", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19026_s035", "title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "chapter": "VIII", "section_number": "35", "section_title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "text": "Act: The motor transport workers act, 1961 (Act 27 of 1961) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VIII: ## PENALTIES AND PROCEDURE | Section 35: Cognizance of offences\n\n**35. Cognizance of offences.—** No court shall take cognizance of any offence under this Act except on complaint made by, or with the previous sanction in writing of, the inspector and no court inferior to that of a Presidency magistrate or a magistrate of the first class shall try any offence punishable under this Act.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1961.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19026?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19026/act.pdf"}
