{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s056", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "56", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: ** | Section 56: Operation of other laws not barred.** - Nothing in this Act shall be deemed to prevent any person fr\n\n**56. Operation of other laws not barred.** - Nothing in this Act shall be deemed to prevent any person from being prosecuted under any other law for the time being in force, for any act or omission which constitutes an offence against this Act or from being liable under such other law to any higher punishment or penalty than that provided by this Act.\n\nProvided that no person shall be punished twice for the same offence.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19151", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19151_s013_2_d16", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(2): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n_containing a declaration that it is for giving effect to such policy shall be called in question in any court on the ground that it does not give effect to such policy:_\n\nProvided that where such law is made by the Legislature of a State, the provisions of this article shall not apply thereto unless such law, having been reserved for the consideration of the President, has received his assent.\n\n> [1] **31D.** [ _Saving of laws in respect of anti-national activities._ ] _Rep. by the Constitution (Forty-third Amendment) Act,_ 1977, _s._ 2 ( _w.e.f._ 13-4-1978).\n\n_Right to Constitutional Remedies_\n\n**32.** (1) The right to move the Supreme Court by appropriate proceedings for the enforcement of the rights conferred by this Part is guaranteed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19151?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19151/act.pdf"}
