{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s203", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIII", "section_number": "203", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIII: ** | Section 203: Breath tests.** - **1** 21[(1) A police officer in uniform or an officer of the Motor Vehicle Depart\n\n**203. Breath tests.** - **1** 21[(1) A police officer in uniform or an officer of the Motor Vehicle Department as may be authorised in this behalf by that Department, may require any person driving or attempting to drive a motor vehicle in a public place to provide one or more specimens of breath for breath test there or nearby, if such police officer or officer has any reasonable cause to suspect him to having committed an offence under section 185:\n\nProvided that requirement for breath test shall be made (unless it is made) as soon as reasonably practicable after the commission of such offence.]", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19151", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19151_s013_4", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(4): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n( _b_ ) any law in force immediately before the commencement of this Constitution in the territory of India with respect to any of the matters referred to in sub-clause ( _i_ ) of clause ( _a_ ) or providing for punishment for any act referred to in sub-clause ( _ii_ ) of that clause shall, subject to the terms thereof and to any adaptations and modifications that may be made therein under article 372, continue in force until altered or repealed or amended by Parliament.\n\n_Explanation._ —In this article, the expression \"law in force\" has the same meaning as in article 372.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19151?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19151/act.pdf"}
