{"act_id": "IND_state_18989", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18989_s212_p0", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "chapter": "XVII", "section_number": "212", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands land revenue and reforms regulation 1966 (Act 2 of 1966) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XVII: Miscellaneous** | Section 212: Notwithstanding anything contained in this Regulation-\n\n212. Notwithstanding anything contained in this Regulation-\n\n(a) all cases pending before the Chief Commissioner or any revenue officer at the commencement of this Regulation shall be disposed of according to the law which would have been applicable to such cases had his Regulation not been passed;\n\n(b) all cases pending before civil court at the commencement of this Regulation which would under this Regulation be triable by a revenue court, shall be disposed of by such civil court according to the law which would have been applicable to such cases had this Regulation not been passed; and\n\n(c)all further proceedings with respect to the cases referred to in clause (a) and (b) whether by way f appeal; revision, review or otherwise, shall be taken or instituted and disposed or according to the law which would have been applicable to such proceedings had this Regulation not been passed.\n\n____________________\n\nTransitory provision.\n\n## **THE SCHEDULE**\n\n_[See Section 2(6)]_\n\n## List Of Commercial Trees\n\n1. White Dhup (Canarium euphyllum)\n\n2. Bakota (Endoperium malaccense)\n\n3. Kadam (Anthocephalus cadmba)\n\n4. Didu or Demul (Bombax insigne)\n\n5. Papita (Sterculia camponulata)\n\n6. Lambapathi (Sideroxylonlon gepetiolatum)\n\n7. Evodia (Evodiaglabra)\n\n8. Red Dhup (Parishis insignis)\n\n9. Lethok (Stercullia alata)\n\n10. Thitpok (Tetrameles nudiflora)\n\n11. Gurjan (Dipterocarpurs spp.)\n\n12. White Chuglam (Terminalia bialate)\n\n13. Badam (Termonalia procera)", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1966.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18989?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18989/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s003_p1", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "3", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ** | Section 3: In section 2 of the principal Act,\n\n� _(12B)_ \"forest produce\" shall have the same meaning as in sub-clause _(b)_ of clause _(4)_ of section 2 of the Indian Forest Act, 1927;';\n\n_(g)_ in clause _(16)_ , for sub-clauses _(a)_ and _(b)_ , the following sub-clauses shall be substituted, namely:\n\n\" _(a)_ killing or poisoning of any wild animal or captive animal and every attempt to do so;\n\n_(b)_ capturing, coursing, snaring, trapping, driving or baiting any wild or captive animal and every attempt to do so;\";\n\n_(h)_ for clause _(18A)_ , the following clause shall be substituted namely:\n\n' _(18A)_ \"livestock\" means farm animals and includes buffaloes, bulls, bullocks, camels, cows, donkeys, goats, sheep, homes, mules, yaks, pigs, ducks, geese, poultry and their young but does not include any animal specified in Schedules I to V;';\n\n_(i)_ for clauses _(19)_ and _(20)_ , the following clauses shall be substituted, namely:-\n\n' _(19)_ \"manufacturer\" means a person who manufactures articles from any animal or plant specified in Schedules I to V and VI, as the case may be;\n\n_(20)_ \"meat\" includes blood, bones, sinew, eggs, shell or carapace, fat and flesh with or without skin, whether raw or cooked, of any wild animal or captive animal, other than a vermin;\n\n_(20A)_ \"National Board\" means the National Board for Wild Life constituted under section 5A;';\n\n_(j)_ after clause _(24)_ , the following clause shall be inserted, namely:", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Indian Forest Act, 1927", "Amendment Act, 2002"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19015", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19015_s009", "title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "text": "Act: The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016 (Act 49 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ## RIGHTS AND ENTITLEMENTS | Section 9: Home and family.** —( _1_ ) No child with disability shall be separated from his or her parents on t\n\n**9. Home and family.** —( _1_ ) No child with disability shall be separated from his or her parents on the ground of disability except on an order of competent court, if required, in the best interest of the child.\n\n( _2_ ) Where the parents are unable to take care of a child with disability, the competent court shall place such child with his or her near relations, and failing that within the community in a family setting or in exceptional cases in shelter home run by the appropriate Government or non-governmental organisation, as may be required.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2016.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19015?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19015/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s212_3", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIV", "section_number": "212", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIV: ** | Section 212(3): Publication, commencement and laying of rules and notifications.** - (1) The power to make rules under this Act is subject to the condition of the rules being made after previous publication\n\n(3) Every rule made by any State Government shall be laid, as soon as may be after it is made, before the State Legislature.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19010", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19010_s025", "title": "The payment of wages act, 1936", "chapter": "", "section_number": "25", "section_title": "The payment of wages act, 1936", "text": "Act: The payment of wages act, 1936 (Act 4 of 1936) | India | State | In Force\nSection 25: Display by notice of abstracts of the Act\n\n**25. Display by notice of abstracts of the Act.—** The person responsible for the payment of wages to persons[1] [employed in a factory or an industrial or other establishment] shall cause to be[2] [displayed in such factory or industrial or other establishment] a notice containing such abstracts of this Act and of the rules made thereunder in English and in the language of the majority of the persons employed[3] [in the factory or industrial or other establishment] as may be prescribed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1936.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19010?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19010/act.pdf"}
