{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s023_d1", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "23", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ** | Section 23: Powers of Collector.** - For the purpose of such inquiry, the Collector may exercise the following powers, namely\n\n**23. Powers of Collector.** - For the purpose of such inquiry, the Collector may exercise the following powers, namely\n\n- (a) the power to enter in or upon any land and to survey, demarcate, and make a map of the same or to authorise any other officer to do so;\n\n- (b) the same powers as are vested in a civil court for the trial of suits.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s086_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "86", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 86: Cancellation and suspension of permits\n\n**86. Cancellation and suspension of permits.-** (1) The Transport Authority which granted a permit may cancel the permit or may suspend it for such period as it thinks fit -\n\n(a) on the breach of any condition specified in section 84 or of any condition contained in the permit, or\n\n(b) if the holder of the permit uses or causes or allows a vehicle to be used in any manner not authorised by the permit, or\n\n(c) if the holder of the permit ceases to own the vehicle covered by the permit, or\n\n(d) if the holder of the permit has obtained the permit by fraud or misrepresentation, or\n\n(e) if the holder of the goods carriage permit, fails without reasonable cause, to use the vehicle for the purposes for which the permit was granted, or\n\n(f) if the holder of the permit acquires the citizenship of any foreign\n\ncountry :\n\nProvided that no permit shall be suspended or cancelled unless an opportunity has been given to the holder of the permit to furnish his explanation.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url