{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s038_p1", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "38", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: ** | Section 38: _**Exemption from certain taxes, fees and duties** :--_ If the Chief Commissioner\n\n**39.** _**Deduction from salary to meet co-operative society's claim in certain -operative society's claim in certain operative society's claim in certain 's claim in certain s claim in certain cases** :-_ (1) Notwithstanding anything contained in any law for the time being in force a member of co-operative society may execute an agreement in such form as may be prescribed in favour of the society providing that his employer or the officer disbursing his salary or wages shall be competent to deduct every month from the salary or wages payable to him, such amount as may be specified in the agreement but not exceeding one-third of the salary or wages and to pay the amount so deducted to the society in satisfaction of any debt or other demand owing by the member to the society.\n\n**Registrar of Co-operative Societies, Co-operative Department, A&N Islands, VIP Road,**\n\n**18**\n\n## **ANDAMAN & NICOBAR GAZETTTE, EXTRAORDINARY, MAY 13, 1973**\n\n[", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s044", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "44", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 44: The word \"or\" omitted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 23 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). 45. Inserted, ibid ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 )\n\n44. The word \"or\" omitted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 23 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). 45. Inserted, ibid ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ).\n\n46. Inserted, ibid ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ).\n\n_**Corresponding Law**_ **:-** Section 71 corresponds to section 47 of the Motor\n\nVehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons**_ **-** Clause 71 lays down the procedure in considering applications for stage carriage permits by the Regional Transport Authorities and also provides for empowering the State Government to issue direction to the Transport authorities to limit the number of stage carriage permits in certain towns and cities with a population of not less than five lakhs.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "general", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor\n\nVehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19012", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19012_s027_p0", "title": "The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "27", "section_title": "The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016", "text": "Act: The real estate (regulation and development) act, 2016 (Act 17 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: THE REAL ESTATE REGULATORY AUTHORITY | Section 27: Restrictions on Chairperson or Members on employment after cessation of office**\n\n**27. Restrictions on Chairperson or Members on employment after cessation of office** .—( _1_ ) The Chairperson or a Member, ceasing to hold office as such, shall not—\n\n( _a_ ) accept any employment in, or connected with, the management or administration of, any person or organisation which has been associated with any work under this Act, from the date on which he ceases to hold office:\n\nProvided that nothing contained in this clause shall apply to any employment under the appropriate Government or a local authority or in any statutory authority or any corporation established by or under any Central, State or provincial Act or a Government Company, as defined under clause ( _45_ ) of section 2 of the Companies Act, 2013 (18 of 2013), which is not a promoter as per the provisions of this Act;\n\n( _b_ ) act, for or on behalf of any person or organisation in connection with any specific proceeding or transaction or negotiation or a case to which the Authority is a party and with respect to which the Chairperson or such Member had, before cessation of office, acted for or provided advice to the Authority;\n\n( _c_ ) give advice to any person using information which was obtained in his capacity as the Chairperson or a Member and being unavailable to or not being able to be made available to the public;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "pr