{"act_id": "IND_state_20096", "chunk_id": "IND_state_20096_s022", "title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "22", "section_title": "The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957", "text": "Act: The Mines and Minerals (Development and Reguation), Act, 1957 (Act 67 of 1957) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: ## MISCELLANEOUS | Section 22: Cognizance of offences** .―No court shall take cognizance of any offence punishable under this Act o\n\n**22. Cognizance of offences** .―No court shall take cognizance of any offence punishable under this Act or any rules made thereunder except upon complaint in writing made by a person authorised in this behalf by the Central Government or the State Government.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1957.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/20096?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_20096/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s001_2_d3", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 1(2): (/) This Act may be called the Wild Life (Protection) Amendment Act, 2006\n\n(2) The Central Government shall remove a member referred to in clause (d) of sub-section (2) of section 38L, from office lfhc-\n\n_(a)_ is, or at a!ly time has been, adjudicated as insolvent;\n\n_(b)_ has been convicted of an offence which, in the opinion of the Central Government, involves moral turpitude;\n\n_(c)_ is of unsound mind and stands so declared by .!l competent court;\n\n(d) refuses to act or becomes incapable of acting;\n\n_(e)_ is, without obtaining leave of absence from the Tiger Conservation Authority, absent from three consecuti.ve meetings of the said Authority; or\n\n_(/)_ has, in the opinion of the Central Government, so abused his position as to render his continuation in office detrimental to the public interest:\n\nProvided that no member shall be removed under this sub-section unless he has been **given a** reasonable opportunity of being heard in the matter.\n\n(J) Any vacancy in the office ofa member shall be filled by fresh appointment and such member shall continue for the remainder of the term of the member In whose place he is appointed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19019", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19019_s19P", "title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "19P", "section_title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "text": "Act: The inland vessels act, 1917 (Act 1 of 1917) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: SURVEY OF INLAND[3] [ MECHNICALLY PROPELLED VESSELS] | Section 19P: Appeals**\n\n**19P. Appeals** .—( _1_ ) Any person aggrieved by an order—\n\n( _a_ ) refusing to register any inland[1] [mechanically propelled vessel] under section 19F;\n\nor\n\n( _b_ ) suspending a certificate of registration under section 19N; or\n\n( _c_ ) cancelling a certificate of registration under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 19-0,\n\nmay, within thirty days of the date on which lie receives notice of such order, appeal against it to the State Government.\n\n( _2_ ) The State Government shall cause notice of every such appeal to be given to the registering authority concerned in such manner as may be prescribed, and after giving an opportunity to that authority and to the appellant to be heard shall pass such order thereon as it thinks fit.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1917.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19019?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19019/act.pdf"}
