{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s025_3", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "25", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 25(3): Transfer of endorsement and issue of driving licence free from endorsement.** - (1) An endorsement o\n\n(3) A person whose driving licence has been endorsed shall, if during a continuous period of three years after such endorsement no further endorsement has been made against him, be entitled on surrendering his driving licence and on payment of a fee of five rupees, to receive a new driving licence free from all endorsements :\n\nProvided that if the endorsement is only in respect of an offence contravening the speed limits referred to in section 112, such person shall be entitled to receive a new driving licence free from such endorsements on the expiration of one year of the date of the endorsement :\n\nProvided further that in reckoning the said period of three years and one year, respectively, and period during which the said person was disqualified for holding or obtaining a driving licence shall be excluded.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 25 corresponds to section 20 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 25 enables the licensing authorities to transfer the endorsements of disqualification to any new or duplicate licences issued to the holder of the licence. It also provides for the issue of fresh driving licence free of endorsements, if during a continuous period of three years from the last endorsement, there has been no further orders of endorsement.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s058_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "58", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 58: Special provisions in regard to transport vehicles. -** (1) The Central Government may, having regar\n\n**58. Special provisions in regard to transport vehicles. -** (1) The Central Government may, having regard to the number, nature and size of the tyres attached to the wheels of a transport vehicle (other than a motorcab), and its make and model and other relevant considerations, by notification in the Official Gazette, specify, in relation to each make and model of a transport vehicle, the 35[maximum gross vehicle weight] of such vehicle and the maximum safe axle weight of each axle of such vehicle.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "order", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s013_2_d17", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "", "section_number": "13", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nSection 13(2): (** 1) All laws in force in the territory of India immediately before the commencement of this Const\n\n(2) The Supreme Court shall have power to issue directions or orders or writs, including writs in the nature of _habeas corpus, mandamus, prohibition, quo warranto_ and _certiorari_ , whichever may be appropriate, for the enforcement of any of the rights conferred by this Part.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19026", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19026_s017", "title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "chapter": "V", "section_number": "17", "section_title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "text": "Act: The motor transport workers act, 1961 (Act 27 of 1961) | India | State | In Force\nChapter V: ## HOURS AND LIMITATIONS OF EMPLOYMENT | Section 17: Split duty\n\n**17. Split duty.—** Subject to the other provisions contained in this Act, the hours of work of a motor transport worker shall not be split into more than two spells on any day.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1961.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19026?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19026/act.pdf"}
