{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s41B_p0", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "41B", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ``` | Section 41B: Compulsory disclosure of information by the occupier. (1)\n\n41B. Compulsory disclosure of information by the occupier. (1)\nThe occupier of every factory involving a hazardous process shall\ndisclose in the manner prescribed all information regarding dangers,\nincluding health hazards and the measures to overcome such hazards\narising from the exposure to or handling of the materials or\nsubstances in the manufacture, transportation, storage and other\nprocesses, to the workers employed in the factory, the Chief\nInspector, the local authority within whose jurisdiction the factory\nis situate and the general public in the vicinity.\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s001_2_d4", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 1(2): (/) This Act may be called the Wild Life (Protection) Amendment Act, 2006\n\n(2) The Tiger Conservation Al!thority moy, in the exercise of its powers and performance of its functions under this Chapter, iHuo directions !n writing to any person, officer or authority for the protection of tiger or tiger reserves and such person, officer or authority shall be bound to comply with the directions:\n\nProvided that no such direction shall interfere with or affect the rights of local people particularly the Scheduled Tribes. 38P. (/) The Tiger Conservation Authority shall meet at such time and at such place as the Chairperson may think tit. (2) Tho Chairperson or in his absence tho Vice-Chairperson shall preside over the meetings of the Tiger Conservation Authority.\n\n(J) The Tiger Conservation Authority shall regulate its own procedure.\n\n( 4) All orders and decisions of the Tiger Conservation Authority shall be authenticated by the Member-Secretary or any other officer of the said Authority duly authorised by the Member-Secretary in this behalf.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18981", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18981_s021_p1", "title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "21", "section_title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "text": "Act: The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 (Act 14 of 1981) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF AIR POLLUTION | Section 21: Restrictions on use of certain industrial plants**\n\nmay be prescribed and where such person makes such application, he shall be deemed to be operating such industrial plant with the consent of the State Board until the consent applied for has been refused.\n\n( _3_ ) The State Board may make such inquiry as it may deem fit in respect of the application for consent referred to in sub-section ( _1_ ) and in making any such inquiry, shall follow such procedure as may be prescribed.\n\n( _4_ ) Within a period of four months after the receipt of the application for consent referred to in sub-section ( _1_ ), the State Board shall, by order in writing,[1] [and for reasons to be recorded in the order, grant the consent applied for subject to such conditions and for such period as may be specified in the order, or refuse such consent]:\n\n2[Provided that it shall be open to the State Board to cancel such consent before the expiry of the period for which it is granted or refuse further consent after such expiry if the conditions subject to which such consent has been granted are not fulfilled:\n\nProvided further that before cancelling a consent or refusing a further consent under the first provision, a reasonable opportunity of being heard shall be given to the person concerned.]\n\n( _5_ ) Every person to whom consent has been granted by the State Board under sub-section ( _4_ ), shall comply with the following conditions, namely:—", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1981.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18981?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18981/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18981", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18981_s018_p0", "title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "18", "section_title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "text": "Act: The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 (Act 14 of 1981) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: POWERS AND FUNCTIONS OF BOARDS | Section 18: Power to give directions.** —[1] [( _1_ )] In the performance of its functions under this Act—\n\n**18. Power to give directions.** —[1] [( _1_ )] In the performance of its functions under this Act—\n\n( _a_ ) the Central Board shall be bound by such directions in writing as the Central Government may give to it; and\n\n( _b_ ) every State Board shall be bound by such directions in writing as the Central Board or the State Government may give to it:\n\nProvided that where a direction given by the State Government is inconsistent with the direction given by the Central Board, the matter shall be referred to the Central Government for its decision.\n\n> 2[( _2_ ) Where the Central Government is of the opinion that any State Board has defaulted in complying with any directions given by the Central Board under sub-section ( _1_ ) and as a result of such default a grave emergency has arisen and it is necessary or expedient so to do in the public interest, it may, by order, direct the Central Board to perform any of the functions of the State Board in relation to such area, for such period and for such purposes, as may be specified in the order.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "order", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1981.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18981?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18981/act.pdf"}
