{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s001_5_d2", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: A** | Section 1(5): (/) This Act may be called the Wild Life (Protection) Amendment Act, 2006\n\n_(g)_ ensure that the tiger ~serves and areas linking one protccied area or tiger reserve with another protected area or tiger reserve are not diverted for ecologically unsustainable uses, ~ept in public interest and with the approval of the Natlonal Board for Wild Life and on the advice of the Tiger Conservation Authority;\n\n(h) facilitate and support the tiger reserve management in the State for biodiversity conservation initiatives through eco-development and people's participation as per approved management plans and to support similar initiatives In a<ljolnlng areas consistent with the Central and State laws;\n\n(() ensure critical support including scientific, information technology and legal support for better Implementation of the tiger conservation plan; _(J)_ facllltate ol)going capacity building programme for skill development of officers and staff of tiger reserves; and\n\n(k) perform such other functions as may be necessary to carry out the purposes of this Act with regard to conservation of tigers and their habitat.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Amendment Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s166_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XII", "section_number": "166", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XII: ** | Section 166: Application for compensation.** - (1) An application for compensation arising out of an accident of the nature specified in sub-section (1) of section 165 may be made -\n\n**166. Application for compensation.** - (1) An application for compensation arising out of an accident of the nature specified in sub-section (1) of section 165 may be made -\n\n(a) by the person who has sustained the injury; or\n\n(b) by the owner of the property; or\n\n(c) where death has resulted from the accident, by all or any of the legal representatives of the deceased; or\n\n(d) by any agent duly authorised by the person injured or all or any of the legal representatives of the deceased, as the case may be :\n\nProvided that where all the legal representatives of the deceased have not joined in any such application for compensation, the application shall be made on behalf of or for the benefit of all the legal representatives of the\n\n99. Added, _ibid_ (w.e.f. 14-11-1994).\n\ndeceased and the legal representatives who have not so joined, shall be impleaded as respondents to the application.\n\n1[(2) Every application under sub - section (1) shall be made, at the option of the claimant, either to the Claims Tribunal having jurisdiction over the area in which the accident occurred or to the Claims Tribunal within the local limits of whose jurisdiction the claimant resides, or carries on business or within the local limits of whose jurisdiction the defendant resides and shall be in such form and contain such particulars as may be prescribed :", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s060_5_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "60", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 60(5): Sub-S. (1) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 29 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (1) read as under \n\n(5) A State Government may prescribe the circumstances under which and the period during which the driver of a vehicle although not engaged in work is required to remain on or near the vehicle may be deemed to be an interval for rest within the meaning of sub-section (1).\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ **-** Section 91 corresponds to section 65 of the motor vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Object and Reasons**_ **. -** Clause 91 prohibits the driving of motor vehicles by a person for more than certain hours in a day and the hours of rest the driver should take after certain hours of continuous driving.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19011", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19011_s007", "title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "7", "section_title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "text": "Act: The plantations labour act, 1951 (Act 69 of 1951) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: INSPECTING STAFF | Section 7: Certifying surgeons**\n\n**7. Certifying surgeons** .—( _1_ ) The State Government may appoint qualified medical practitioners to be certifying surgeons for the purposes of this Act within such local limits or for such plantation or class of plantations as it may assign to them respectively.\n\n- ( _2_ ) The certifying surgeon shall carry out such duties as may be prescribed in connection with—\n\n( _a_ ) the examination and certification of workers;\n\n( _b_ ) the exercise of such medical supervision as may be prescribed where adolescents[1] [are], employed in any work in any plantation which is likely to cause injury to their health.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1951.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19011?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19011/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s050_3", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "50", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 50(3): Transfer of ownership.** - (1) Where the ownership of any motor vehicle registered under this Chapter is transferred. -\n\n(3) Any entry made under sub - section (1) or sub - section ( 2), may be cancelled by the 26[ last registering authority ] on proof of the termination of the said agreement by the parties concerned on an application being made in such form as the Central Government may prescribe 27 [ and an intimation in this behalf shall be sent to\n\nthe original registering authority if the last registering authority is not the original registering authority.]", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s049_7", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "49", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: AUDIT, INQUIRY, INSPECTION AND SURCHARGE** | Section 49(7): _**Inspection of co-operative societies**_ :- (1) The Registrar, or any person\n\n(7) Audit fee, if any, due from any co-operative society shall be recoverable in\n\nthe same manner as is provided in section 67.\n\n49. _**Inspection of co-operative societies**_ :- (1) The Registrar, or any person\n\nauthorised by the Registrar by general or special order in this behalf, may inspect a co-operative society.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
