{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s033_p1", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "33", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ## ESTABLISHMENT OF BOARDS AND THEIR FUNCTIONS | Section 33: Powers of inspection by Chief Executive Officer or persons authorised by him\n\n( _2_ ) Whenever any such inspection as referred to in sub-section ( _1_ ) is made, the concerned mutawalli and all officers and other employees working under him and every person connected with the administration of the[1] [waqf], shall extend to the person making such inspection, all such assistance and facilities as may be necessary and reasonably required by him to carry out such inspection, and shall also produce for inspection any movable property or documents relating to the[1] [waqf] as may be called for by the person making the inspection and furnish to him such information relating to the[1] [waqf] as may be required by him.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf"}
