{"act_id": "IND_state_18993", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18993_s023_p0", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Marine Fishing Regulation, 2003", "chapter": "I", "section_number": "23", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Marine Fishing Regulation, 2003", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Marine Fishing Regulation, 2003 (Act 1 of 2003) | India | State | In Force\nChapter I: PRELlMINAllY | Section 23: (1) No suit, prosecution or other legal proceeding shall lie against the Administrator or any office\n\n23. (1) No suit, prosecution or other legal proceeding shall lie against the Administrator or any officer or authority for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in pursuance of this Regulation or any order or rule made thereunder.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2003.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18993?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18993/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19320", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19320_s033", "title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "33", "section_title": "The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972", "text": "Act: The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 (Act 53 of 1972) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ** | Section 33: Control of sanctuaries.** - The Chief Wildlife Warden shall be the authority who shall control, manage and maintain all sanctuaries and for that purpose, within the limits of any sanctuary,\n\n**33. Control of sanctuaries.** - The Chief Wildlife Warden shall be the authority who shall control, manage and maintain all sanctuaries and for that purpose, within the limits of any sanctuary,\n\n- (a) may construct such roads, bridges, buildings, fences or barrier gates, and carry out such other works as he may consider necessary for the purposes of such sanctuary;\n\n- (b) shall take such steps as will ensure the security of wild animals in the sanctuary and the preservation of the sanctuary and wild animals, therein;\n\n- (c) may take such measures, in the interests of wildlife, as he may consider necessary for the improvement of any habitat.\n\n- (d) may regulate, control or prohibit, in keeping with the interests of wildlife, the grazing or movement of [livestock].\n\n- (e) [omitted 19911\n\n**[[9] 3** 3 **A. Immunisation of livestock.** -(41) The Chief Wildlife Warden shall take such measures in such manner as may be prescribed, for immunisation against communicable diseases of the livestock kept in or within five kilometres of a sanctuary. (2) No person shall take, or cause to be taken or graze, any livestock in a sanctuary without getting it immunised.]", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1972.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19320?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19320/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s087_2_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "87", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 87(2): Temporary permits. -** (1) A Regional Transport Authority and the State Transport Authority may with\n\n## **88. Validation of permits for use outside region in which granted. -**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s150_4", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XI", "section_number": "150", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XI: ** | Section 150(4): Rights of third parties against insurers on insolvency of the insured.** - (1) Where under any contr\n\n(4) Upon a transfer under sub-section (1) or sub-section (2), the insurer shall be under the same liability to the third party as he would have been to the insured person, but -\n\n(a) if the liability of the insurer to the insured person exceeds the liability of the insured person to the third party, nothing in this Chapter shall affect the rights of the insured person against the insurer in respect of the excess, and\n\n(b) if the liability of the insurer to the insured person is less than the liability of the insured person to the third party, nothing in this Chapter shall affect the rights of the third party against the insured person in respect of the balance.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 150 corresponds to section 97 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 150 provides that in the event of the insured becoming insolvent any liability incurred by the insured person and his rights against the insurer will be transferred to and vest in the third party to whom the liability was so incurred.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s002_ii_d1", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "2", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 2(ii): Interpretation\n\n(ii) in any scheduled employment under the control of any Government in India in respect of which minimum rates of wages have been fixed under this Act, the person or authority appointed by such Government for the supervision and control of employees or where no person or authority is so appointed, the head of the department;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "general", "section_type": "definition_clause", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1948", "Factories Act, 1934"], "defined_terms": ["adolescent", "adult", "appropriate government", "child", "competent authority", "employee", "employer", "prescribed", "scheduled employment", "wages"], "amendment_count": 2, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19151", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19151_s001_3_d8", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: .—SPECIAL DIRECTIVES | Section 1(3): to entertain and dispose of appeals and petitions from or in respect of any judgment, decree or order of any court within that State shall cease, and all appeals and other proceedings pending before the said authority at such commencement shall be transferred to, and disposed of by, the Supreme Court.\n\n( _Part XXI._ — _Temporary, Transitional and Special_\n\n## _Provisions_ .— _Art._ 371 _D_ .)\n\n## (4) An order made under clause (3) may—\n\n( _a_ ) authorise the Administrative Tribunal to receive representations for the redress of grievances relating to any matter within its jurisdiction as the President may specify in the order and to make such orders thereon as the Administrative Tribunal deems fit;\n\n( _b_ ) contain such provisions with respect to the powers and authorities and procedure of the Administrative Tribunal (including provisions with respect to the powers of the Administrative Tribunal to punish for contempt of itself) as the President may deem necessary;\n\n( _c_ ) provide for the transfer to the Administrative Tribunal of such classes of proceedings, being proceedings relating to matters within its jurisdiction and pending before any court (other than the Supreme Court) or tribunal or other authority immediately before the commencement of such order, as may be specified in the order;\n\n( _d_ ) contain such supplemental, incidental and consequential provisions (including provisions as to fees and as to limitation, evidence or for the application of any law for the time being in force subject to any exceptions or modifications) as the President may deem necessary.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Bombay Reorganisation Act, 1960", "Nagaland Act, 1962", "India Act, 1935", "States Reorganisation Act, 1956", "The Indian Independence Act, 1947", "Privy Council Jurisdiction Act, 1949"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19151?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19151/act.pdf"}
