{"act_id": "IND_state_19313", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19313_s008", "title": "The Indian Forest Act 1927", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "8", "section_title": "The Indian Forest Act 1927", "text": "Act: The Indian Forest Act 1927 (Act 16 of 1927) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: OF RESERVED FORESTS | Section 8: Powers of Forest Settlement-officer.** —For the purpose of such inquiry, the Forest Settlementofficer may exercise the following powers, that is to say:—\n\n**8. Powers of Forest Settlement-officer.** —For the purpose of such inquiry, the Forest Settlementofficer may exercise the following powers, that is to say:—\n\n( _a_ ) power to enter, by himself or any officer authorised by him for the purpose, upon any land, and to survey, demarcate and make a map of the same; and\n\n- ( _b_ ) the powers of a Civil Court in the trial of suits.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1927.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19313?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19313/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18981", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18981_s021_p3", "title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "21", "section_title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "text": "Act: The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 (Act 14 of 1981) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF AIR POLLUTION | Section 21: Restrictions on use of certain industrial plants**\n\n( _c_ ) after the erection or re-erection of any chimney under clause ( _iv_ ),\n\nno control equipment or chimney shall be altered or replaced or, as the case may be, erected or re-erected except with the previous approval of the State Board.\n\n( _6_ ) If due to any technological improvement or otherwise the State Board is of opinion that all or any of the conditions referred to in sub-section ( _5_ ) require or requires variation (including the change of any control equipment, either in whole or in part), the State Board shall, after giving the person to whom\n\n> 1. Subs. by Act 47 of 1987, s. 9, for certain words (w.e.f. 1-4-1988).\n\n> 2. Ins. by s. 9, _ibid_ . (w.e.f. 1-4-1988).\n\n> 3. The words \"for the purpose of any industry specified in the Schedule\" omitted by s. 9, _ibid_ . (w.e.f. 1-4-1988).\n\nconsent has been granted an opportunity of being heard, vary all or any of such conditions and thereupon such person shall be bound to comply with the conditions as so varied.\n\n( _7_ ) Where a person to whom consent has been granted by the State Board under sub-section ( _4_ ) transfers his interest in the industry to any other person, such consent shall be deemed to have been granted to such other person and he shall be bound to comply with all the conditions subject to which it was granted as if the consent was granted to him originally.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc