{"act_id": "IND_state_18984", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18984_s052", "title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "52", "section_title": "The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012", "text": "Act: The andaman and nicobar islands excise regulati0n, 2012 (Act 3 of 2012) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ## ExCISE REVENUE | Section 52: Whoever, attempts to commit any offence punishable under this Regulation, shall be liable for half the punishment provided for the offence under this Regulation\n\n52. Whoever, attempts to commit any offence punishable under this Regulation, shall be liable for half the punishment provided for the offence under this Regulation.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['tax_law', 'property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2012.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18984?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18984/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s104", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "104", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: or any rule made thereunder section 87 has resulted in an\naccident causing death or serious bodily injury, the fine shall not be\nless than 2*[twenty five thousand] in the case of an accident causing\ndeath, and 2*[five thousand rupees] in the case of an accident causing\nserious bodily injury.\nExplanation.--In this section and in section 94 \"serious bodily\ninjury\" means an injury which involves, or in all probability will\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Ins. by Act 20 of 1987, s. 29 (w.e.f. 1-12-1987)\n2. Subs. by s. 30, ibid. (w.e.f. 1-12-1987).\n3. Ins. by Act 94 of 1976 s. 40, (w.e.f. 26-10-1976).\n``` | Section 104: Onus as to age. (1) When any act or omission would, if a\n\n104. Onus as to age. (1) When any act or omission would, if a\nperson were under a certain age, be an offence punishable under this\nAct, and such person is in the opinion of the Court prima facie under\nsuch age, the burden shall be on the accused to prove that such person\nis not under such age.\n88D\n(2) A declaration in writing by a certifying surgeon relating to\na worker that he has personally examined him and believes him to be\nunder the age stated in such declaration shall, for the purposes of\nthis Act and the rules made thereunder, be admissible as evidence of\nthe age of that worker.\n104A\n```\n\n```\nOnus of proving limits of what is practicable, etc.\n```\n\n```\n1*[104A. Onus of proving limits of what is practicable, etc. In\nany proceeding for an offence for the contravention of any provision\nof this Act of rules made thereunder consisting of a failure to comply\nwith a duty or requirement to do something, it shall be for the person\nwho is alleged to have failed to comply with such duty or requirement,\nto prove that it was not reasonably practicable or, as the case may\nbe, all practicable measures were taken to satisfy the duty or\nrequirement.]\n105.\nCognizance of offences.\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s095_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "95", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 95: Power of State Government to make rules as to stage carriages**\n\n**95. Power of State Government to make rules as to stage carriages**\n\n**and contract carriages -** (1) A State Government may make rules to regulate, in respect of stage carriages and contract carriages and the conduct of passengers in such vehicles.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing provision, such rules may -\n\n(a) authorise the removal from such vehicle of any person contravening the rules by the driver or conductor of the vehicle, or, on the request of the driver or conductor, or any passenger, by any police officer ;\n\n(b) require a passenger who is reasonably suspected by the driver or conductor of contravening the rules to give his name and address to a police officer or to the driver or conductor on demand.\n\n(c) Require a passenger to declare, if so demanded by the driver or conductor, the journey he intends to take or has taken in the vehicle and to pay the fare for the whole of such journey and to accept any ticket issued therefor ;\n\n(d) Require, on demand being made for the purpose by the driver or conductor or other person authorised by the owners of the vehicle, production during the journey and surrender at the end of the journey by the holder thereof of any ticket issued to him ;\n\n(e) Require a passenger, if so requested by the driver or conductor, to leave the vehicle on the completion of the journey the fare for which he has paid ;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s017_2", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "17", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 17(2): Minimum time rate wages for piece work\n\n(2) Every employer shall keep exhibited, in such manner as may be prescribed, in the factory, workshop or place where the employees in the scheduled employment may be employed, or in the case of outworkers, in such factory, workshop or place as may be used for giving out-work to them, notices in the prescribed form containing prescribed particulars. --------------------------------------------------------------------1. Subs. by Act 26 of 1954, s. 4, for \"section 47 of the Factories Act, 1934\". 211", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1934"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s010", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "10", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 10: Resolution for Amendment** :- No amendment under rule 9 shall be carried out save in accordance with\n\n**10. Resolution for Amendment** :- No amendment under rule 9 shall be carried out save in accordance with a resolution passed at a general meeting of the cooperative society of which due notice or the intention to discuss the amendment in the meeting has been given to its members.\n\n**46**\n\n## **ANDAMAN & NICOBAR GAZETTTE, EXTRAORDINARY, OCT, 16, 1974**\n\nProvided that no such resolution shall be valid unless it is passed by a majority of members present at the general meeting at which not less than two third of members for the time being of the co-operative society are present:\n\nProvided further that amendment of bye-laws on the lines of model byelaws previously approved by the Registrar may be adopted by a majority at an ordinary general meeting.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s214_2", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIV", "section_number": "214", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIV: ** | Section 214(2): Effect of appeal and revision on orders passed by**\n\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), if an application made by a person for the renewal of permit has been rejected by the original authority and such person has preferred an appeal or made an application for revision under this Act against such rejection, the appellate authority or, as the case may be, the revisional authority may by order direct that the permit shall, notwithstanding the expiration of the term specified\n\ntherein, continue to be valid until the appeal or application for revision is disposed of,", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "order", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19011", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19011_s18A_p0", "title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "18A", "section_title": "The plantations labour act, 1951", "text": "Act: The plantations labour act, 1951 (Act 69 of 1951) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ## WELFARE | Section 18A: Safety\n\n**18A. Safety.—** ( _1_ ) In every plantation, effective arrangements shall be made by the employer to provide for the safety of workers in connection with the use, handling, storage and transport of insecticides, chemicals and toxic substances.\n\n( _2_ ) The State Government may make rules for prohibiting or, restricting employment of women or adolescents in using or handling hazardous chemicals.\n\n( _3_ ) The employer shall appoint persons possessing the prescribed qualifications to supervise the use, handling, storage and transportation of insecticides, chemicals and toxic substances in his plantation.\n\n( _4_ ) Every employer shall ensure that every worker in plantation employed for handling, mixing, blending and applying insecticides, chemicals and toxic substances, is trained about the hazards involved in different operations in which he is engaged, the various safety measures and safe work practices to be adopted in emergencies arising from spillage of such insecticides chemicals and toxic substances and such other matters as may be prescribed by the State Government.\n\n( _5_ ) Every worker who is exposed to insecticides, chemicals and toxic substances shall be medically examined periodically, in such manner as may be prescribed, by the State Government.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1951.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19011?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19011/act.pdf"}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19019", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19019_s056", "title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "chapter": "VII", "section_number": "56", "section_title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "text": "Act: The inland vessels act, 1917 (Act 1 of 1917) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VII: PENALTIES AND LEGAL PROCEEDINGS | Section 56: Penalty for neglect to affix certificate of survey in inland mechanically propelled. vessel**\n\n**56. Penalty for neglect to affix certificate of survey in inland mechanically propelled. vessel** .—If the certificate of survey is not kept affixed in an inland[1] [mechanically propelled vessel] as required by section. 10,[3] [or if the registration mark is not displayed as required by section 19H], the owner and the\n\n> 1. Subs. by Act 35 of 1977, s. 5, for \"steam-vesse1\" (1-5-1978).\n\n> 2. Ins. by Act 26 of 1951, s. 4.\n\n> 3. Ins. by s. 5, _ibid._\n\nmaster of the[1] [mechanically propelled vessel] shall each be punishable with fine which may extend to one hundred rupees.\n\n> 2 [ **57. Penalty for neglect or refusal to deliver up or surrender certificates of survey or registration** .—If the owner or master of an inland 1[mechanically propelled vessel] without reasonable cause neglects or refuses—\n\n( _a_ ) to deliver up a certificate of survey when required under section 14 so to do; or\n\n( _b_ ) to ,deliver up a certificate of registration when required under section 19N so to do; or\n\n( _c_ ) to surrender a certificate of registration as required by section 190;\n\nhe shall be punishable with fine, which may extend to one hundred rupees.]", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_refere